   "evidence": "Lines 351-357: `have h2 : \u221a2 ^ 2 = 2 := Real.sq_sqrt zero_le_two` / `rw [minkowskiProduct_axisVector_left]` / `simp [axisVector, basis_apply]` / `field_simp` / `linear_combination (s * t - 1) * h2`. Contrast line 346-349, where `minkowskiProduct_axisVector_left` uses an explicit `simp only [...]` terminated by `ring` \u2014 the robust form the same file already demonstrates.",
   "file": "EpsilonEridani/Relativity/LightConeBasis.lean",
   "fix": "Make the component values explicit \u2014 add private lemmas `axisVector_apply_inl : axisVector i s (Sum.inl 0) = (\u221a2)\u207b\u00b9` and `axisVector_apply_inr : axisVector i s (Sum.inr i) = s * (\u221a2)\u207b\u00b9`, rewrite with them instead of `simp [axisVector, basis_apply]`, and close with `field_simp` + `ring` using the named fact `Real.mul_self_sqrt (zero_le_two)` (or `h2`) rather than a tuned `linear_combination` coefficient. Replacing the bare `simp` with a `simp only [...]` naming the lemmas used is the minimum.",
   "issue": "`minkowskiProduct_axisVector` (351-357) runs `rw`, then a non-terminal `simp [axisVector, basis_apply]` using the default simp set, then `field_simp`, then `linear_combination (s * t - 1) * h2`. Both the goal reaching `field_simp` and the one reaching `linear_combination` are invisible, and the coefficient `(s*t-1)` is tuned to whatever normal form `field_simp` produces, so any upstream simp-set change breaks it silently. This lemma is load-bearing: all four `minkowskiAxis` structure fields (365-368) go through it.",
   "line": "351"
  }
